menu "PEAR MIB Configuration"

    choice PEAR_DHCP_MODE
        prompt "Ethernet DHCP mode"
        default PEAR_DHCP_SERVER
        help
            The joystick HMI (pace-hmi-fw) is a DHCP client. On a direct cable
            between the HMI and this board (the chair topology, no router) this
            board must hand out the address: DHCP server, 192.168.4.1/24. On a
            bench LAN with a router, use DHCP client so the PC tools
            (rtps_mcb_gui.py etc.) share one subnet with both boards.

        config PEAR_DHCP_SERVER
            bool "DHCP server (192.168.4.1/24) - direct cable to the HMI"
        config PEAR_DHCP_CLIENT
            bool "DHCP client - bench LAN with a router"
    endchoice

endmenu
